A||N||5||Dan87GT||Which AC Compressor to Buy?||||1||
Z||000000||Dan87GT||07-10-2001||08:31 AM||||I am doing a R134 upgrade to my 86SE and need a new AC compressor. I am not sure which one to buy, there are several listed fro it i.e. H6, DA-6 etc. Any thoughts or part #'s||||reg||1
Z||000001||Voytek||07-10-2001||01:57 PM||||Up here Napa has told me to use the DA6.  Apparently the DA6 is not recommended after the 4th month in '87 (I am not sure why - the guy didn't know either).  I also assume you have the V6 (I do).<BR>Hey, just out of curiosity - how much do they want for one of those down there?  Here they want $250-$260 CDN (that's the lowest price in town).<BR>Also, why are you replacing it?  You don't need to if you're just doing the conversion.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Dan87GT||07-10-2001||03:15 PM||||Thanks, the cheapest I have found for a rebuild is $240 so far. I am not positive mine is shot but I disconnected the belt back in 1990 or so. So I have a feeling that its junk. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||07-11-2001||12:49 PM||||I used a new Delco DA-6 on my 85SE v-6 4spd.  It cost around $335 US.  Rebuilt ones were around $185 US.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Voytek||07-11-2001||02:00 PM||||OUCH!  That's pretty steep!  But I guess the $185 US is somewhat comparable to the $250/$260 CDN I'm quoted up here.  BTW, it's also a rebuild.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Leadfoot||07-11-2001||02:14 PM||||I think Napa gave me the wrong compressor.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  They gave me a DA-4.  Looked identical to the old one.  I already swapped the switches over.  Anyone know if this is a problem?  The compressor is off a 85 2m6.||||reg||1
